+# Comment Escape browser check
+
+Requires Cargo, Chrome and `playwright-cli`. Build from the checkout, start a fresh
+throwaway daemon and make the fixture from the map recipe (substitute your scratch
+paths and port):
+
+```sh
+cargo build --locked --target-dir /tmp/jelly-escape-target
+/tmp/jelly-escape-target/debug/jelly serve --port 17883 --home /tmp/jelly-escape-home
+# In another terminal, from the checkout:
+/tmp/jelly-escape-target/debug/jelly --url http://127.0.0.1:17883 new escape:map --from skill/recipes/map
+```
+
+From a scratch directory, run the check with an absolute path to the script:
+
+```sh
+playwright-cli -s=escape open http://127.0.0.1:17883/
+playwright-cli -s=escape run-code --filename=/path/to/jelly/tests/comment-escape.js
+playwright-cli -s=escape close
+```
+
+It walks a map trace to step 3, turns on commenting and presses Escape, standalone
+and inside the jelly page's full view. Commenting must end while the trace keeps its
+step, and a second Escape must leave the trace. It also checks that Escape in the
+comment editor closes it without moving the trace. Both Escape checks fail on the
+pre-fix runtime. Stop the throwaway daemon afterward.
+
